text:
found it. after a socket drop the client reconnects but the events buffered during the gap never get flushed. `onReconnect` re-subscribes but doesn't call `flushQueue()`. section B's subnet kills idle sockets after ~60s so they hit it constantly
```
socket.on('reconnect', () => {
  subscribe(sessionId)
  // missing: flushQueue(sessionId)
})
```
Reactions: scream (2)
